Subject: [PATCH] xre: use the system Mozilla directory the distribution has

The system directory for native-messaging hosts and system extensions
(/usr/lib64/mozilla or /usr/lib/mozilla) is fixed when the engine is built,
from its libdir. Fedora packages put hosts such as KeePassXC-Browser and
Plasma Browser Integration in /usr/lib64/mozilla; Debian and Ubuntu use
/usr/lib/mozilla. With one Nulavio build for both families, the engine
keeps the build-time directory when it exists and otherwise uses the other
one that exists. Both are root-owned system locations; nothing in the
user's home is involved.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not applicable (distribution packaging choice).
---
--- a/toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/xre/nsXREDirProvider.cpp
@@ -352,6 +352,24 @@
 #    endif
       ;
   rv = NS_NewNativeLocalFile(dirname, getter_AddRefs(localDir));
+#    if defined(XP_LINUX)
+  // Nulavio: one build for Fedora and Debian/Ubuntu. Use whichever system
+  // directory the distribution actually has (Fedora: /usr/lib64/mozilla,
+  // Debian/Ubuntu: /usr/lib/mozilla); keep the build-time default when
+  // neither exists. Both are root-owned system locations.
+  bool exists = false;
+  if (NS_SUCCEEDED(rv) && (NS_FAILED(localDir->Exists(&exists)) || !exists)) {
+    for (const auto& candidate :
+         {"/usr/lib64/mozilla"_ns, "/usr/lib/mozilla"_ns}) {
+      nsCOMPtr<nsIFile> other;
+      if (NS_SUCCEEDED(NS_NewNativeLocalFile(candidate, getter_AddRefs(other))) &&
+          NS_SUCCEEDED(other->Exists(&exists)) && exists) {
+        localDir = other;
+        break;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+#    endif
 #  endif
 
   if (NS_SUCCEEDED(rv)) {
